pped. Black, flake8 and mypy also pass on the project.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`sqlite_utils/create_table_parser.py` (new):** the stdlib-only lexer and parser. It provides `Check`, `ColumnComments`, `ParseError`, `parse_checks`, `parse_column_comments`, `check_references_identifier`, `rewrite_check_expression` and `sql_ends_in_line_comment`, plus the SQLite keyword list.\n- **`sqlite_utils/db.py`:**\n  - `Table.checks`, `column_checks` and `table_checks`.\n  - `create_table_sql` takes keyword-only `_checks` and `_column_comments`.\n  - `transform_sql` carries checks and comments into the rebuilt table. It renames columns inside CHECK expressions and refuses to drop a column that a remaining CHECK uses. Nothing is executed before that check runs.\n\n**Choices I made where the spec was open**\n- `parse_column_comments` returns `{}` for anything that isn't a `CREATE TABLE`, including virtual tables. I read \"Not a CREATE TABLE body: `{}`\" as non-raising, unlike `parse_checks`, which raises `ParseError`. Invalid tokens such as an unterminated comment still raise.\n- Any double-quoted token anywhere in a CHECK expression makes `options` `None`, so `\"col\" IN ('a')` gets no options.\n- `_column_definition_with_comments` accepts `None` and returns the definition unchanged, so every column goes through it.\n- I added a bare `*` before `_checks` so the two new parameters are keyword-only. Existing positional callers are unaffected.\n- A `# assert` narrows a regex match that mypy could not prove non-None. It is guaranteed by the branch that calls it.\n\n**Not done**\n- I did not commit. `SPEC.md` is still untracked, as it was at the start.\n- `ty check` from the Justfile was not run because it isn't installed in the offline environment.", "ttft_ms": 2752, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 305586, "uuid": "81368b8b-36bd-4a29-8f17-7b7f26892ae5", "ttft_stream_ms": 2482, "time_to_request_ms": 310, "first_content_frame_ms": 2483, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
